    "notes": [
      {
        "text": "All information products included in [https://github.com/cisagov/CSAF/tree/develop/csaf_files/IT/white](https://github.com/cisagov/CSAF/tree/develop/csaf_files/IT/white) are provided \\\"as is\\\" for informational purposes only. The Department of Homeland Security (DHS) does not provide any warranties of any kind regarding any information contained within. DHS does not endorse any commercial product or service, referenced in this product or otherwise. Further dissemination of this product is governed by the Traffic Light Protocol (TLP) marking in the header. For more information about TLP, see [https://us-cert.cisa.gov/tlp/](https://us-cert.cisa.gov/tlp/).",
        "title": "Legal Notice",
        "category": "legal_disclaimer"
      },
      {
        "text": "Worldwide",
        "title": "Countries and Areas Deployed",
        "category": "other"
      },
      {
        "text": "Information Technology",
        "title": "Critical Infrastructure Sectors",
        "category": "other"
      },
      {
        "text": "OpenJDK and many downstream Java implementations do not securely decode Base64 data when x86 or x64 CPU AVX-512 extensions are enabled. An attacker with the ability to control Base64 input may be able to manipulate heap memory to cause a Java process to crash or execute arbitrary code. In many cases attacks can be attempted remotely and without authentication. Oracle Java SE, Oracle GraalVM for JDK, and Oracle GraalVM Enterprise Edition are affected.",
        "title": "Risk Evaluation",
        "category": "summary"
      },
      {
        "text": "Fixed in OpenJDK and Oracle Java SE 17.0.21.1, 21.0.13.1, 25.0.5.1, and 27.0.1.1, Oracle Java SE 8u513-perf (Java SE 17.0.21.1), Oracle GraalVM for JDK 17.0.21.1 and 21.0.13.1, and Oracle GraalVM Enterprise Edition 21.3.20.1.",
        "title": "Recommended Practices",
        "category": "general"
      },
      {
        "text": "United States",
        "title": "Company Headquarters Location",
        "category": "other"
      }
    ],
